message.content:
This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   The user's single request (verbatim): "Migrate every route and file from the Pages Router to the Next.js App Router. When finished, remove the pages dir entirely. Ensure the proper App Router APIs are used. If a Pages Router API was used that no longer exists in App Router, replace it with the newer version or the new pattern. Make sure to add types."

   Project instructions (CLAUDE.md → AGENTS.md) that constrain how the work must be done, verbatim: "# This is NOT the Next.js you know — This version has breaking changes — APIs, conventions, and file structure may all differ from your training data. Read the relevant guide in `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before writing any code. Heed deprecation notices." I complied by reading the bundled version-matched docs before writing any code.

   No security-relevant constraints, credential rules, or forbidden operations were stated by the user beyond the above.

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Next.js 16.4.0-canary.20 (verified via node_modules/next/package.json), React 19.1.0, TypeScript 5, Turbopack default
   - App Router file conventions: `layout.tsx`, `page.tsx`, `route.ts`, `not-found.tsx`, `error.tsx`, `loading.tsx`
   - Async Request APIs (breaking in v16): `params`, `searchParams`, `headers()`, `cookies()`, `draftMode()` are Promises; sync access fully removed
   - `error.js` **`retry`** prop (stable v16.3.0) replaces the older `reset` idiom; error boundaries must be Client Components; no `metadata` export allowed → use React `<title>`
   - `getServerSideProps` → async Server Component + `headers()` from `next/headers`
   - `getStaticProps` + `revalidate` → route segment config `export const revalidate = N` (ISR); valid because `cacheComponents` is NOT enabled
   - `getStaticPaths` → `generateStaticParams`; `fallback: 'blocking'` → `export const dynamicParams = true`
   - `fetch` is **not** cached by default in v16 ("auto no cache"; caching is opt-in via `force-cache`/`next.revalidate`)
   - `next/head` → Metadata API (`metadata` object / `generateMetadata` returning `Metadata`)
   - `pages/_app.js` + `pages/_document.js` → single root `app/layout.tsx` (must define `<html>`/`<body>`; no manual `<head>`)
   - `pages/404.js` → `app/not-found.tsx`; `pages/_error.js` → `app/error.tsx`; `router.isFallback` → `loading.tsx`
   - `useRouter` from `next/navigation` (no `pathname`/`query`/`isFallback`/`asPath`); React Context providers need `'use client'`
   - `pages/api/*` → Route Handlers; undefined HTTP methods automatically return 405 with `Allow`
   - Google Fonts `<link>` → `next/font/google` with `variable` CSS var, self-hosted at build
   - `next typegen` global helpers (`PageProps`, `LayoutProps`, `RouteContext`) exist but I deliberately used explicit inline Promise types to avoid depending on generated types
   - Other v16 changes noted but not applicable here: `middleware`→`proxy`, `revalidateTag(tag, profile)`, `updateTag`/`refresh`, PPR→`cacheComponents`, removal of `next lint`/AMP/runtime config

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - **AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md** (read only): mandated reading `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before coding.

   - **Docs read** (all under `/home/sandbox/workspace/node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/`): `02-guides/migrating/app-router-migration.md`, `02-guides/upgrading/version-16.md`, `03-api-reference/03-file-conventions/{page,layout,route,not-found,error}.md`, `.../02-route-segment-config/{index,dynamicParams}.md`, `03-api-reference/04-functions/{generate-static-params,use-router,generate-metadata,headers,userAgent,fetch,not-found}.md`, `01-getting-started/{06-fetching-data,11-css,02-project-structure}.md`, `02-guides/incremental-static-regeneration.md`, `03-api-reference/02-components/font.md`.

   - **lib/posts.ts** (created) — shared typed data access for jsonplaceholder, avoids scattered casts:
     ```ts
     const API_URL = 'https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com'

     export interface Post { userId: number; id: number; title: string; body: string }
     export interface PostComment { postId: number; id: number; name: string; email: string; body: string }

     export async function getPosts({ limit }: { limit?: number } = {}): Promise<Post[]> {
       const res = await fetch(limit ? `${API_URL}/posts?_limit=${limit}` : `${API_URL}/posts`)
       if (!res.ok) { throw new Error(`Failed to fetch posts: ${res.status}`) }
       return (await res.json()) as Post[]
     }
     export async function getPost(id: string): Promise<Post | null> {
       const res = await fetch(`${API_URL}/posts/${id}`)
       if (!res.ok) { return null }
       return (await res.json()) as Post
     }
     export async function getComments(postId: string): Promise<PostComment[]> {
       const res = await fetch(`${API_URL}/posts/${postId}/comments`)
       if (!res.ok) { throw new Error(`Failed to fetch comments: ${res.status}`) }
       return (await res.json()) as PostComment[]
     }
     ```

   - **components/AppProvider.tsx** (created, replaces deleted components/AppProvider.js) — Context must be a Client Component:
     ```tsx
     'use client'
     import { createContext, useContext, useState } from 'react'
     import type { Dispatch, ReactNode, SetStateAction } from 'react'
     export type Theme = 'light' | 'dark'
     export interface AppContextValue { theme: Theme; setTheme: Dispatch<SetStateAction<Theme>> }
     const AppContext = createContext<AppContextValue | null>(null)
     export function AppProvider({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {
       const [theme, setTheme] = useState<Theme>('light')
       return (<AppContext.Provider value={{ theme, setTheme }}>{children}</AppContext.Provider>)
     }
     export function useAppContext(): AppContextValue {
       const context = useContext(AppContext)
       if (!context) { throw new Error('useAppContext must be used within AppProvider') }
       return context
     }
     ```

   - **components/NavButton.tsx** (created) — `'use client'`, `useRouter` from `next/navigation`, `<button type="button" onClick={() => router.push(href)}>`; props `{ href: string; children: ReactNode }`. Used by home, blog index, not-found.

   - **components/BackButton.tsx** (created) — `'use client'`, `router.back()`; props `{ children: ReactNode }`.

   - **app/layout.tsx** (created; replaces `_app.js` + `_document.js`):
     ```tsx
     import type { Metadata } from 'next'
     import { Inter } from 'next/font/google'
     import Link from 'next/link'
     import type { ReactNode } from 'react'
     import { AppProvider } from '@/components/AppProvider'
     import '@/styles/globals.css'

     // Replaces the Google Fonts <link> tags that used to live in `_document.js`:
     // the font is downloaded at build time and self-hosted.
     const inter = Inter({ subsets: ['latin'], display: 'swap', variable: '--font-inter' })

     export const metadata: Metadata = {
       title: 'My Blog',
       description: 'A complex blog application',
       icons: { icon: '/favicon.ico' },
     }

     export default function RootLayout({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {
       return (
         <html lang="en" className={inter.variable}>
           <body>
             <AppProvider>
               <div className="app-container">
                 <header><h1>My Blog</h1><nav><Link href="/">Home</Link><Link href="/blog">Blog</Link></nav></header>
                 <main>{children}</main>
